    "created_at": "2016-10-11T17:08:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-11T17:08:02Z",
    "body": "I think we don't need to have double-bracket notation to have internal slots. IMO the existing \"that is cancelable\" is a way of setting the already-existing implicit cancelable internal slot. (Most places would state this as \"associated cancelable flag\", but I guess DOM does not at the moment.)\n\nI don't feel strongly either way though, and I see you've already made the changes in #1886 in your preferred direction, so I'm happy to go along with that. Will try to review that later today.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
